    "chunk_text": "(b)upon the death of such member;\n\n(c)upon such member resigning from such office bywriting addressed to the President; or\n\n(d)on the expiration of the term of the Committee andthe consequent expiration of a member\u2019s term ofoffice.\n\n(10) Where the implementation of any recommendationhas not been fully complied with, the reports of theCommittee shall include the reasons for non-implementationas provided by the persons or organisations responsible forthe implementation thereof.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n35Commission for Truth, Unity andReconciliation in Sri Lanka\n\nPART IX\n\nGENERAL\n\n41. The members of the Commission (for the limitedpurpose of their functions under the Act) and the officersand staff of the Commission shall be deemed to be \u201cpublicofficers\u201d for the purposes of the Penal Code (Chapter 19),the Anti-Corruption Act, No. 9 of 2023 and the EvidenceOrdinance (Chapter 14).\n\n42. The Commission shall be deemed to be a \u201cscheduledinstitution\u201d within the meaning of the Anti-Corruption Act,No. 9 of 2023, and the provisions of that Act shall beconstrued accordingly.\n\n43. No member of the Commission or officer or memberof the staff of the Commission shall make private use of, orprofit from, any confidential information gained as a resultof such member\u2019s work in the Commission, or divulge suchinformation to any other person except in the course of hisfunctions as a member of the Commission or officer ormember of the staff of the Commission. This obligation shallsurvive the expiration of the term of the Commission.\n\n44. Each Member of the Commission or officer or memberof the staff of the Commission shall act impartially andwithout conflict of interest. Accordingly, such member,officer or staff member shall avoid taking any action whichcould create an appearance of partiality or undermine theintegrity of the Commission.\n\nMembers oftheCommissionto be deemedpublicofficers\n\nCommissionto be deemeda sc