    "chunk_text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE RUBBER CONTROL ACT\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Rubber Control(Amendment) Act, No. of 2024.\n\n(2) Every reference to the \u201cController\u201d and \u201cRubberController\u201d in any other written law or in any notice,notification, contract, communication form, other instrumentor document shall from and after the date of the coming intooperation of this Act be read and construed as a referencemade to the \u201cDirector-General of the Rubber DevelopmentDepartment\u201d.\n\n3. Section 26 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed.\n\n4. The heading appearing immediately after the wordsand figure \u201cPART VI\u201d of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following heading substituted therefor: -\n\n\u201cRUBBER ADVISORY BOARD\u201d\n\nShort title\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nGeneralAmendmentto Chapter436 and anyother writtenlaw\n\nRepeal ofsection 26 ofthe principalenactment is\n\nReplacementof heading inPart VI of theprincipalenactment\n\n2Rubber Control (Amendment)\n\n5. Sections 36, 37, 38, 39, 39A and 50 of the principalenactment are hereby repealed.\n\n6. Section 52 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the repeal of the definition of \u201cController\u201d, andthe substitution therefor, of the following new definition :-\n\n\u2018\u201cDirector-General\u201d means the Director-General ofthe Rubber Development Department,appointed or deemed to have been appointedunder this Act;\u201d.\n\n7. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n5\n\n10Sinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency\n\nRepeal ofsections 36,37, 38,39,39A and 50of theprincipalenactment\n\nAmendmentof section 52of theprincipalenactment\n\nRubber Control (Amendment)3\n\nDepartment of Government Printing"
